; Part of ferrum. MIT licence, see ferrum/LICENSE.
; FIND single edge (ferrum's FRONT EDGE). The probe starts at probing depth
; beside the front face, within #3018 of it, and moves +Y to touch
; it once (o<ferrum_edge>: fast touch, back off #3019, slow touch). The
; edge is the contact plus the effective tip radius #5410 / 2 - #3032 and
; is reported as y_plus_probed_position / #1008. With #3030 = 0
; the active work offset's Y is set so that the edge reads 0; no other
; axis is written. No Z motion. Ends #3019 off the face at the same Z, with
; the modal state as it was.
o<probe_y_plus_wco> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<probe_y_plus_wco> return
o10 endif
o<ferrum_probe_ready> call
M73
M50 P0
G90 G94
o<ferrum_edge> call [1] [1] [#3018]
o20 if [#3030 EQ 0]
    G10 L20 P0 Y[#5421 - #<_ferrum_edge>]
o20 endif
o<probe_y_plus_wco> endsub
M2
